                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "175af2df-ee89-30a7-85da-8f0ca6f45bf9",
                        "entry_id": "5035da8a-88a1-3d0a-94c8-d1e370dfebaa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "female equivalent of вестовщи́к (vestovščík): female newsmonger"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "feminine",
                            "form-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c1c05b3-695d-4d56-8445-76a73b8a8e22",
                                "sense_id": "175af2df-ee89-30a7-85da-8f0ca6f45bf9",
                                "text": "Обе́дал почти́ всегда́ у коменда́нта, где обыкнове́нно проводи́л оста́ток дня и куда́ вечерко́м иногда́ явля́лся оте́ц Гера́сим с жено́ю Акули́ной Памфи́ловной, пе́рвою вестовщи́цею во всём около́тке.",
                                "translation": "I invariably dined at the commandant's, where I usually passed the rest of the day, and occasionally Father Gherassim, with his wife Akoulina Pamphylovna, the great tale-bearer in the neighbourhood, used to spend the evening with us.",
                                "english": "I invariably dined at the commandant's, where I usually passed the rest of the day, and occasionally Father Gherassim, with his wife Akoulina Pamphylovna, the great tale-bearer in the neighbourhood, used to spend the evening with us."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
